From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:24:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: pasemi: Recover from a late interrupt and a stale
 received byte

On the iPad 6, a PMIC read during resume from s2idle could take the bus down
for good. The read ended with "Timeout, status 0x08090118": XEN set and XIP
clear, so the transfer had finished and its byte was in the receive FIFO,
only the completion interrupt was late. The caller got an error and the byte
stayed behind.

The next transfer then found MRNE set and reset the controller, but on T8010
the reset carries no FIFO flush bits (ctl_flags is 0) and nothing read the
byte out. Each following read returned the answer before its own: "Issuing
reset due to status 0x00090118" on every transfer and a mismatched read-back
on every charger input-limit write, with no bus error logged, so USB and
charging stayed dead until a reboot.

Fix both ends. A transfer whose status says it finished is treated as
finished, and the status checks that follow still count its errors. When the
status says the FIFO holds data, read it empty, bounded in case the empty
flag never comes.

Why the interrupt is late during resume is not known yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pasemi-core.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pasemi-core.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pasemi-core.c
index c3f0daba77d2..4d554ff9adfc 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pasemi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-pasemi-core.c
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@
  */
 #define PASEMI_TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_MS	100
 
+/* Far more than any FIFO here holds: an empty flag that never comes must not hang. */
+#define PASEMI_RX_DRAIN_MAX		256
+
 static inline void reg_write(struct pasemi_smbus *smbus, int reg, int val)
 {
 	dev_dbg(smbus->dev, "smbus write reg %x val %08x\n", reg, val);
@@ -107,6 +110,22 @@ static void pasemi_begin_xfer(struct pasemi_smbus *smbus)
 	reinit_completion(&smbus->irq_completion);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Empty the receive FIFO. Not every integration flushes it on a reset (T8010
+ * runs without the legacy CTL flush bits), and a byte left behind makes every
+ * later read return the answer before its own, for good.
+ */
+static unsigned int pasemi_drain_rx(struct pasemi_smbus *smbus)
+{
+	unsigned int drained;
+
+	for (drained = 0; drained < PASEMI_RX_DRAIN_MAX; drained++)
+		if (RXFIFO_RD(smbus) & MRXFIFO_EMPTY)
+			break;
+
+	return drained;
+}
+
 static int pasemi_smb_clear(struct pasemi_smbus *smbus)
 {
 	unsigned int status;
@@ -133,6 +152,9 @@ static int pasemi_smb_clear(struct pasemi_smbus *smbus)
 			 "Issuing reset due to status 0x%08x (xfstatus 0x%08x)\n",
 			 status, reg_read(smbus, REG_XFSTA));
 		pasemi_reset(smbus);
+		if (status & SMSTA_MRNE)
+			dev_warn(smbus->dev, "Drained %u stale received bytes\n",
+				 pasemi_drain_rx(smbus));
 	}
 
 	/* Clear the flags */
@@ -159,9 +181,14 @@ static int pasemi_smb_waitready(struct pasemi_smbus *smbus)
 				"Completion wait failed with %d, status 0x%08x\n",
 				ret, status);
 			return ret;
-		} else if (ret == 0) {
+		} else if (ret == 0 && !(status & SMSTA_XEN)) {
 			dev_err(smbus->dev, "Timeout, status 0x%08x\n", status);
 			return -ETIME;
+		} else if (ret == 0) {
+			/* It finished; only its interrupt is late. */
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(smbus->dev,
+					     "Late completion interrupt, status 0x%08x\n",
+					     status);
 		}
 	} else {
 		ret = readx_poll_timeout(ioread32, smbus->ioaddr + REG_SMSTA,
